00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,160
Chapter 9, S or Z. S is hissed. Z is buzzed. Most S's are pronounced as Z's.

2
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:17,080
The sound of the letter S is S only if it follows an unvoiced consonant. Otherwise,

3
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:23,500
it becomes a Z in disguise. When an S follows vowel, a voiced consonant, or

4
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,700
another S, it turns into a Z. The following exercise will let you hear and

5
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:33,920
practice S with its dual sound. There are many more Z sounds in English than S

6
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:34,400
sounds.
